<title>USA: EXAR takes big Q4 charge, sees flat revs.</title>
<headline>EXAR takes big Q4 charge, sees flat revs.</headline>
<dateline>FREMONT, Calif. 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>EXAR Corp said on Wednesday it will take a pretax restructuring charge of $8 million to $10 million in the fourth quarter of fiscal 1997, and expects revenues to be flat in this quarter and possibly the next.</p>
<p>The charge results in part from the company's decision to reduce its workforce by 12 percent and transfer its test and shipping operations to offshore sub-contractors.</p>
<p>The company expects revenues to be flat in the near term while it repositions itself to focus efficiently on core strengths.</p>
</text>
